[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The iMac screen in the palm of your hand. That\'s exactly what I was thinking when I got them—Rayneo GT Max. The idea of ​​having a huge portable screen wherever I went sounded pretty crazy. And combined with micro-LED'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'screens that deliver up to 120 hertz, being able to play games on them was something I didn\'t expect at all. So, are they really worth it? Hello everyone , welcome back to my channel, where I talk about'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'technology and gadgets, as well as my experience using them , going beyond the specifications. And this is my very first pair of AR glasses. Frankly , Rayneo sent them to me in exchange for this review. They wanted me to cover a few technical'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'specifications, but I\'m allowed to criticize, and of course, my experiences and opinions are my own . In this video, I\'ll talk about my experience with them over the past month, including all the devices I tested them on, their technical'

[00:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'performance, and ultimately, what I decided to do with them , which may surprise you given my initial thoughts on smart glasses. I really didn\'t have high expectations before starting. In my opinion, AR glasses still had three main problems.'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'They are bulky and not very portable. The screens are probably not of very good quality. And honestly, why not just buy a tablet if your goal is to watch movies? Maybe it\'s because when I think of any device in this space,'

[01:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I still picture those bulky VR headsets from a decade ago . So when they arrived in one tiny box, I was surprised, to say the least. I was expecting some kind of mini power supply, something like the Apple Vision'

[01:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Pro. But these glasses only use a single USB-C to USB-C cable, and as it turns out, that\'s all it takes. I usually tend to be overly protective of my things. If I have a backpack with a'

[01:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'special laptop compartment, I\'ll still buy a soft case just in case. But this case is so sturdy that I really would n\'t feel guilty throwing them on top of a travel'

[01:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bag. The glasses themselves have a hard plastic body. They are quite dense, but not as heavy as I expected: 78 grams for the Max version. The material to the touch inspires confidence that these glasses will be'

[02:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'quite durable. The hinges work very smoothly and softly, and I have n\'t had any problems in the last month of use. Most of the weight of these glasses is concentrated at the front, where the screens are located.'

[02:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here you will find micro- OLED panels with a brightness of up to 1200 nits and a contrast ratio of 200,000 to 1. More on that later. You\'ll also find this dark shielding that serves as a mini backdrop for whatever'

[02:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'content you\'re watching. In the middle of the device are rubber nose pads and the ability to install lenses with diopters. I actually wear glasses every day, so for me, a person with severe astigmatism, this is a very nice option.'

[02:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There are convenient buttons on the right bracket that switch between three screen modes: fixed, tracking, or stable. And on the left is a set of buttons for adjusting the volume'

[02:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and controlling the main menu. Overall, navigating the settings of these glasses is quite fast and responsive, with a very user-friendly interface. Right out of the box, they have an ultra-wide 59° field of view with an'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'adjustable screen size of up to 307 inches. Thanks to the Vision 4000 display chip, these screens support Dolby Vision via Pocket TV and HDR conversion, just in case 1200 nits isn\'t'

[03:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'enough for you. But with a product like this, specifications are only half the battle. What are they in real use? Honestly, for me, many of the features that were managed to fit into this device are'

[03:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'redundant. During the entire month of using GT Max, I was never able to raise the brightness above 80-90% in most scenarios. I tested these glasses in different places and at different times:'

[03:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'during the day on the couch, in the office in the morning, and at night in bed. It never occurred to me that I needed even more brightness. The Zone 360 ​​feature and spatial tracking are a nice addition'

[03:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'when you want to stay in the same position with the screen. And the image quality is generally fantastic. Even though it\'s an OLED screen, I didn\'t expect the quality to be this high. Black remains truly'

[04:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'deep, and colors have a nice saturation without being overly bright . From the beginning, I leaned towards the standard mode because it provided the best color accuracy. The speakers are also surprisingly great.'

[04:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Enabling Bang&amp; Olufsen mode gives a noticeable bass boost . The audio system, combined with head tracking and spatial audio, gives the Max a much wider soundstage. The image quality and'

[04:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'clarity are also very good if you want to use this as an all-purpose solution. I watched most of The Return of the King exclusively in these glasses over the course of several evenings. Of course, since these are external speakers and not headphones, you won\'t'

[04:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'get any isolation from outside noise. But I suspect a lot of people will use them with AirPods or full-size noise-canceling headphones on airplanes. It\'s actually very difficult to show'

[04:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the feeling of Air glasses on video, because a lot depends on the ambient lighting, the size of the screen in the raeneo menu, and the distance to the wall. But the best way I can describe it is this. Imagine you are sitting in your'

[05:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'local movie theater . You took the best seat in the hall, right in the middle. It\'s a daytime show, and the film has been running for several months. At this point, you are one of ten or twelve people who came to'

[05:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'see the movie that day . At night, when I\'m lying in bed or on the couch in the office, these are exactly the feelings these glasses sometimes give . It\'s like I have the entire movie theater at my disposal. And that feeling is pretty cool. These glasses'

[05:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work with any device that provides image output and power via USB-C. That last part is important because it means your Android phone, iPhone, or Steam Deck will be able to power the GT Max, but the Nintendo Switch won\'t,'

[05:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as it won\'t output a picture without a dock. Also worth noting if you\'re a beginner: this isn\'t full-fledged virtual reality, so you retain some of the benefits of peripheral vision. So, if you'

[05:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are in an environment where you need to be aware of what is going on around you, like on a plane or train, I consider this an advantage. One advantage of having all the processing happen off- device is that you can'

[06:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'use the glasses right out of the box without any setup. You can watch videos on YouTube, Netflix, or any other local media from your gallery right from your phone, laptop, or tablet. By the way, if you\'re interested, you'

[06:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can just plug them into any computer you use. In my case, it\'s a MacBook connected to a monitor that serves as an additional external display. Now I have a whole'

[06:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'virtual screen hanging in front of my eyes, and it\'s actually really cool because, again , you keep a wide peripheral field of vision when you have these glasses on. And of course, if you want to play video games incognito, you can,'

[06:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which brings me to my most controversial thought: Rain X should show games more often in their promotional materials, because connecting these glasses to a laptop is just'

[06:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'incredible. I connected them to my Steam Deck OLED, and it really feels like these two devices were made for each other. The ability to combine the power and portability of a Steam Deck with a movie screen is a'

[07:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'real breakthrough, but there are a few things to keep in mind. First, if you, like'

[07:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'me, are a little sensitive to headaches or dizziness due to low viewing angles or motion blur in video games, I strongly recommend playing with " pin mode" enabled and the brightness of your glasses turned down. I noticed that these'

[07:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'settings helped me adapt better and not feel so nauseous from motion sickness. Secondly, it may be a Steam OS issue, but my Steam Deck did not recognize the headset speakers, even though they worked flawlessly on all other platforms'

[07:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '. Android, iOS, Mac. This is a bit of a shame, because I would really like to play Forza with the surround sound that these glasses provide. I\'ve tested several different games from many genres and can highlight a few important'

[07:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'observations. Although the glasses support a frequency of up to 120 hertz, running games with lower frame rates, especially in graphically complex projects, does not feel as " slow" as on a regular monitor. While playing Elden Ring on the'

[08:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Steam Deck at an average of 40–50 FPS, it felt just as fast as it did at 120 Hz. Overall, the gaming experience on these glasses is great, and thanks to the wired connection, we get the benefits of'

[08:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the low display latency and rich colors of the micro OLED. During testing, I also found that third-person games felt a little more immersive than first- person games. It\'s also worth noting that depending'

[08:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on where you\'re playing —on the couch, in an office chair, or lying in bed—your perception of screen size will change based on what\'s in your peripheral vision. You\'ll also notice some blurring of clarity'

[08:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if you\'re not looking directly at the center of the screen, but during my personal tests I only caught quick glances at the game\'s UI elements in combat, though your experience may vary. So, this video was originally going to be an integrated'

[08:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ad segment for another one I was working on that was a little longer. However, I had so many thoughts about these glasses and AR in general that I decided it would be more useful to share these impressions with first-time buyers and those'

[09:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'looking for a new model. I liked these glasses so much that the next time I go on vacation, I will definitely take them with me in my carry-on luggage . Before GT Maxes appeared, I was completely indifferent to this product and'

[09:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this entire category, but over the past few weeks I\'ve watched so many videos about this niche and new interesting developments that I think it\'s worth paying attention to. If, like me, you were n\'t at all interested in'

[09:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'AR glasses, you might want to keep an eye on developments, because with the industry developing at such a rapid pace, something might appear in the near future that will catch your attention, even if it\'s not these glasses.'
